# Two keys and you are running:
#
#   export ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=sk-ant-...
#   export TAVILY_API_KEY=tvly-...
#   uv run python -m superforecaster serve
#
# This file exists for when you want them to persist, or when you are deploying.
# Real environment variables win over anything set here.

# ---------- the two keys ----------

# The model. console.anthropic.com
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=

# Web search, used by every research agent. Free tier at tavily.com.
# Without it the agents fall back to Wikipedia alone — the run still completes, but the
# reference classes it finds are noticeably thinner, and the header says so.
TAVILY_API_KEY=

# Route the model through the Logfire Gateway instead of calling Anthropic directly.
# logfire.pydantic.dev -> org -> Gateway. Legacy paig_... keys no longer work.
# PYDANTIC_AI_GATEWAY_API_KEY=

# ---------- only when you deploy this ----------

# Required to start a forecast from anywhere other than localhost. Unset, the API accepts
# unauthenticated admin requests from 127.0.0.1 and refuses them from everywhere else —
# which is what makes the two-key local setup work. Set it before exposing the port.
# ADMIN_API_KEY=

# ---------- optional ----------

# AGENT_MODEL=anthropic:claude-sonnet-4-6      # override the model for every agent
# LOGFIRE_TOKEN=                               # pylf_v1_... write token for cloud traces
# DATABASE_PATH=./superforecaster.db           # Docker uses /app/data/superforecaster.db

# Search budget per cell — one column of the grid at one research stage.
# CELL_SOFT_CALLS_PER_ITERATION=1              # the cline: converge past this many
# CELL_HARD_HEADROOM=3                         # calls between the cline and the wall

# Search budget for the criteria critic. Two searches, three is the wall — a
# resolvability review is one or two lookups, and past that it is forecasting the
# question rather than judging its wording.
# CRITIQUE_SOFT_CALLS=2
# CRITIQUE_HARD_HEADROOM=1

# Tool calls for the agents outside the forecast graph: the resolution check, the daily
# update, the post-mortem.
# MONITOR_TOOL_CALLS=4

# Deadlines. A usage limit bounds how many times an agent may act; these bound how long
# it may take. Every stall this system has produced was a request that never came back,
# which reaches no limit and raises nothing — so without these a run never ends and the
# browser sits on a loading state forever. Set any of them to 0 to disable.
# AGENT_TIMEOUT_SECONDS=180                    # one agent run
# RUN_TIMEOUT_SECONDS=1200                     # a whole forecast run
# RUN_WATCHER_GRACE_SECONDS=45                 # cancel a run nobody is watching. The
#                                              # window absorbs an SSE reconnect; 0 means
#                                              # runs continue after the tab closes.

# REFRESH_CRON_SCHEDULE=0 6 * * *
# DIGEST_CRON_SCHEDULE=0 9 28-31 * *
# MIN_PROBABILITY_DELTA=0.03
# SEARCH_LOOKBACK_HOURS=48
